module PipelineBareLambdaOperand exposing (..)


-- A pipeline step whose operand is a BARE (unparenthesized) multi-line lambda.
-- Its head stays on the `|>`'s row and only its body moves, which is what
-- `>>`, `++`, a user-defined operator and `<|` all do with the same operand,
-- and what the PARENTHESIZED twin below has always done. It is excluded from
-- the trigger split by `isDirectGluedOperand`, alongside the paren and bracket
-- operands.
--
-- It used to be the one operand kind missing from that exclusion, so it became
-- the step's trigger and left the preamble empty -- `|>` alone on its row with
-- the lambda a tab stop below it, a shape gren-format emitted nowhere else.
-- (The operator is a Box prefix over the operand, so "empty preamble" means
-- "nothing shares the operator's row"; rendering that as a flow of zero items
-- is what crashed with `box: empty flow` before it was made a blank line.)
--
-- The bare `if`, `when` and `let` operands are the same rule, added the same
-- day: they were the last operand kinds that still emptied the preamble. `>>`,
-- `++` and a user-defined operator glue a bare block's head too (measured), and
-- so has `|> (if …)`, the parenthesized spelling of this very operand, from the
-- beginning. elm-format reaches the glued shape by ADDING the parens --
-- divergence #34 -- which gren does not do.
--
-- The multi-line STRING at the bottom is the fifth, and it is why this list is
-- worth reading as a list. It was still missing after the four above were
-- added, and nothing in this corpus held a `|> """` until gen-random's
-- stranded-operator oracle produced 42 seeds of it. `++ """` and `>> """`
-- glue it, and so does the parenthesized twin, so `|>` was again the only
-- operator that did not.
--
-- The string is NOT part of divergence #34, unlike the lambda and the block: a
-- string is an atom, so elm-format does not parenthesize it, and elm-format's
-- output for `bareMultilineStringGluesToo` is byte-identical to this one
-- (checked against the binary). Here the fix moved gren onto elm-format rather
-- than away from it.
--
-- The last declaration pins the fix's SCOPE: with something already in the
-- preamble the string is a plain argument, so it breaks the call the way any
-- other author-broken call breaks -- one argument per row. `isDirectGluedOperand`
-- cannot fire there, and that is by construction, not by a second rule.


bareLambda =
    a
        |> b
        |> \decoder -> f decoder
        |> c


parenLambdaStaysGlued =
    a
        |> (\decoder ->
                f decoder
           )
        |> c


recordOperandStaysGlued =
    a
        |> { rec
           | x = 1
           , y = 2
           }


bareIfGluesToo =
    a
        |> if c then
            x

           else
            y


bareWhenGluesToo =
    a
        |> when c is
            Just w ->
                w

            Nothing ->
                y


bareLetGluesToo =
    a
        |> let
            q =
                1
           in
           q


bareMultilineStringGluesToo =
    a
        |> """
           one
           two
           """
        |> c


parenMultilineStringStaysGlued =
    a
        |> ("""
            one
            two
            """
           )


multilineStringAfterOtherOperandsDoesNotGlue =
    a
        |> fn arg
            """
            one
            """
